        <body>
            <div xml:id="d103">

                <pb facs="0255" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg181"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>No record of this meeting has been found. The only reference to the discussion is
                    in the Churchill telegram of January 12, 1942 (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >post</hi>, <ref target="#pg399">p. 399</ref>) from which it appears that
                    Roosevelt took up the question of <pb facs="0256" n="182" xml:id="pg182"/> St.
                    Pierre–Miquelon on an urgent basis, that Churchill agreed to the Hull formula of
                    January 8 (<hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg393">p.
                    393</ref>), and that Churchill proposed to bring pressure on de Gaulle to accept
                    it.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
